{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/774325-changeling-question-where-do-new-sidhe-come-from","id":774325,"title":"Changeling Question: Where do new Sidhe come from?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-25T15:39:01-08:00","id":774325,"title":"Changeling Question: Where do new Sidhe come from?","content":"okay, so it's been stated several times that the sidhe do not reincarnate like other changelings. So how do new sidhe childlings keep popping up in the modern day. Only a certain number came through after the moonlanding, do they breed true? if they aren't reincarnating, then shouldn't they all be grumps by now? Especially puzzling given their vulnerability to banality, its a wonder that there are any sidhe left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T18:32:07-08:00","id":774442,"title":"","content":"They do reincarnate if they've undergone The Changeling Way. There's a great FAQ here: <a href=\"http://www.oocities.org/timessquare/portal/8632/errata.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.oocities.org/timessquare/...32/errata.html</a>.<br /> <br /> There are also sidhe still being exiled from Arcadia, although fewer than in previous years. <br /> <br /> What we don't really know is what happens to the human souls the sidhe booted from their bodies when they first arrived back in the Autumn World. Some say they're in Arcadia. Others say they're cast adrift in the Dreaming, hungry for revenge. The Time of Judgment supplement includes options for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T06:31:35-08:00","id":775431,"title":"","content":"Seconding what Adambeyoncelowe said. There's still a slow, but steady trickle of new sidhe arriving. Also, some like the Scathach underwent the changeling way. There's nothing saying others haven't done the same or might in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:38:40-08:00","id":775791,"title":"","content":"I expect we will see some changes in c20 as most of the gamelines went out of their way to make things more playable and less guilting you for playing a snowflake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T14:01:56-08:00","id":777357,"title":"","content":"I think the classic explanation for Sidhe childlings is that not all the Sidhe who came over during the Resurgence incarnated at the same time. While the real world is unbearably devastating to their glamour-bodies, time isn't always quite the same to them. So arrival is spread out over time as well as space, leaving Returned Sidhe available to pop up any time after the Resurgence.<br /> <br /> <br /> I never followed Wraith much, but wasn't there a clan/kith/whatever-equivalent of them that were not dead, but instead people who could astral project? It might be interesting, if so, to have a pair of twins: one is a Sidhe childling, and the other an astral projector whose Shadow is actually the evicted soul his Sidhe brother stole the body from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T00:06:56-08:00","id":778151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/774325-changeling-question-where-do-new-sidhe-come-from?p=777357#post777357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never followed Wraith much, but wasn't there a clan/kith/whatever-equivalent of them that were not dead, but instead people who could astral project? It might be interesting, if so, to have a pair of twins: one is a Sidhe childling, and the other an astral projector whose Shadow is actually the evicted soul his Sidhe brother stole the body from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orpheus had projectors, if that's what you're getting at.<br /> <br /> In Denizens of the Dreaming, there are also fae beings who seem inextricably tied to the Underworld, as if they're ghosts who died in the Dreaming (or human spirits evicted from their mortal shells by the sidhe...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}